# Beads — hard lock (`br` only, never `bd`)

This project uses **beads_rust** for local issue tracking. The CLI binary is **`br`**.

This rule is **always applied** and is **installed into every client repo** by
`agentic-tool install` (pre-rule) and refreshed on every `apply` (all `core/rules/**`).
Host sync projects it to `.cursor/rules/` / `.claude/rules/` (etc.). Every installed
agent persona also restates this hard lock.

## Hard rule

- **Always use `br`** (beads rust / beads_rust) for beads commands.
- **Never use `bd`** — that is the legacy beads CLI and is **not** supported in this pipeline.
- If docs, memory, or another agent suggest `bd`, **correct to `br`** before running anything.
- Triage / robot output uses **`bv`** (`bv --robot-triage`, `bv --robot-*`) alongside `br`.

## Canonical commands

```bash
bv --robot-triage              # what to work on next
br ready                       # unblocked tasks
br show <id>
br create "..." --parent <epic-id>
br update <id> --status=in_progress
br close <id> --reason="..."
br sync --flush-only           # export to .beads/issues.jsonl for git
```

## Boundaries

| System | Tracks |
|--------|--------|
| **`br` / `.beads/`** | Issues, dependencies, close reasons |
| **`_code_agent/`** | Pipeline step progress (checkpoints) |

Planning (Phase 6), per-task implementation, and closeout (Phase 10) all run through **`br`**.
